<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Badis ibn al-Mansur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/989">989</a>–<a href="/years/1016">1016</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Badis ibn al-Mansur was the Zirid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> from 996 to 1016, ruling as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>. He placed his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammad-ibn-buluggin">Hammad ibn Buluggin</a> in charge of the western lands, but in 1015 Hammad broke away and founded the independent Hammadid dynasty. Badis died in 1016 while besieging Hammad's fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qalat-beni-hammad">Qal'at Beni Hammad</a>.</p></div>
